From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 07:53:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] images: let a padded gralloc.waydroid take over from
 gralloc.default

Without a render node Android renders in software, through ANGLE on
lavapipe or through Mesa, and either way llvmpipe draws. llvmpipe works
in 4x4 blocks and assumes its render targets are padded to whole
blocks. gralloc.default allocates the exact height, rounded to a page.
Blending a window whose height is 2 more than a multiple of 4 then
reads past the end of the buffer.

On the BraX3 that covers its full-screen and most app windows: 720x1390,
720x1462 and 720x1470. SurfaceFlinger died with SEGV_ACCERR in llvmpipe's
blend code 11 times in a day, taking every open app with it.

A distribution can install a gralloc.waydroid.so into the vendor
overlay: gralloc.default with those rows allocated, and nothing else
changed. hw_get_module() loads it only when ro.hardware.gralloc is
unset, as it then tries gralloc.<ro.board.platform>.so, and that is
"waydroid". So drop ro.hardware.gralloc=default when that module is
there. The hwcomposer and stagefright read an unset value as "default",
and the buffers still are gralloc.default's.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [LuneOS-specific: needs the padded gralloc module LuneOS ships]
---
 tools/helpers/images.py | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tools/helpers/images.py b/tools/helpers/images.py
index 2c78879..c89cd48 100644
--- a/tools/helpers/images.py
+++ b/tools/helpers/images.py
@@ -202,6 +202,19 @@ def make_prop(args, cfg, full_props_path):
         props.append("ro.hardware.egl=angle")
         props.append("ro.hardware.vulkan=lvp")
 
+    # Software rendering is llvmpipe either way, and llvmpipe works in 4x4
+    # blocks that run past the bottom of a gralloc.default buffer whose height
+    # is not a multiple of 4: SurfaceFlinger dies reading the rows that are not
+    # there. gralloc.waydroid, where a distribution installs it into the vendor
+    # overlay, is gralloc.default with those rows allocated. Android loads it
+    # in place of gralloc.default once ro.hardware.gralloc is unset, as
+    # hw_get_module() then tries gralloc.<ro.board.platform>, which is
+    # "waydroid". The hwcomposer and stagefright read an unset value as
+    # "default", which is what the buffers still are.
+    if "ro.hardware.gralloc=default" in props and \
+            vendor_has("hw/gralloc.waydroid.so"):
+        props.remove("ro.hardware.gralloc=default")
+
     def add_prop(key, cfg_key):
         value = cfg[cfg_key]
         if value != "None":
-- 
